      <rules>
        <rule name="Storm Caller" id="c2d9-e78d-6164-44c8" hidden="false">
          <description>In the Shooting phase of any Space Wolve&apos;s turn, the Rune Priest can use this psychic powers to call up a blizzard of psychic energy which can be used to hide friendly troops from the enemy. He may not shoot on the same turn that he calls up the storm. If successful he summons a storm over himself and the unit he is with, or over any friendly unit that has a model within 12&quot; of him. The unit counts as being in cover for rules purposes and so will receive a 5+ cover save and will strike first in close combat until the end of the following enemy turn. A unit protected in this way may assault, and if they do so against an enemy that are also in cover the attacks are resolved in order of Initiative.</description>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="true">
              <conditions>
                <condition childId="2682-a24d-27d0-d11d" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </rule>
      </rules>
